  itemDescription: Disability Research Institute  The Disability Research Institute
    is dedicated to improving the lives of people with disabilities through research
    and innovation. It focuses on rehabilitation medicine, assistive technologies,
    and inclusive design. Key areas include developing prosthetics and orthotics
    (in collaboration with Bioengineering), studying therapies for disabilities (e.g.
    physical therapy, speech therapy improvements), and disability prevention strategies.
    The institute also addresses social and educational inclusion, aiming to inform
    policies that empower individuals with disabilities. Its mission is to turn scientific
    research into practical solutions that enhance mobility, communication, and independence
    for disabled persons
